<title>SINGAPORE: Uraco 1995/96 net profit rises 24 pct.</title>
<headline>Uraco 1995/96 net profit rises 24 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to July 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     15.38 vs  12.40</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)			1.00 vs   0.75</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     5.24 vs   5.51</p>
<p>    Turnover				116.49 vs  84.19</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 1.29 vs   1.43</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     22.84 vs  18.93</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.97 vs   1.02</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	   6.83 vs   3.81</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	     0.19 vs   0.02</p>
<p>    Tax					 0.19 vs   1.06</p>
<p>    Minorities		     (gain) 0.35 vs   0.65 (loss)</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:    February 4, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open:  January 26, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Uraco Holdings Ltd is a precision engineering company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
